## Base model license (benchmark of the local adapter, F1c)

The exploratory adapter benchmark (`lce_validation/bench_adapter.py`) fine-tunes
Qwen/Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct as its base model. That model is distributed under the
Qwen RESEARCH license (non-commercial; see the LICENSE file in the model card).
No adapter weights are distributed in this repository: they can be regenerated
from the committed recipe (about 36 seconds on the author's machine), and the
SHA-256 of the local checkpoints is recorded in
`results/bench_adapter/adapter_mara/MANIFEST_WEIGHTS.json`. A regenerated adapter
is functionally equivalent but not guaranteed to be bit-identical (MLX training
is not deterministic); the manifest is how to check. The
alternative for a commercial-compatible base is a permissively licensed model
(Apache-2.0/MIT), recorded in the next-phase design.
